- ## Why Camoufox Over Chrome
- | Signal | Chrome/Playwright | Camoufox |
- |--------|-------------------|----------|
- | headless detection | Easily detected | Undetectable |
- | navigator.webdriver | Set when automated | Blocked at C++ level |
- | WebGL fingerprint | Reports virtual GPU | Spoofed to match Firefox |
- | AudioContext | Distinct pattern | Spoofed |
- | User-Agent | Chrome headless marker | Realistic Firefox 152.0 |
- | Screen geometry | Reports small headless size | Normal screen pattern |
- ## Server
- The Camoufox browser server runs on port 9377 by default. It starts automatically with OpenClaw Gateway (`autoStart: true`). Startup can be verified via health endpoint: `http://localhost:9377/health`
- ## Setup Dependencies
- # Server creates browser tabs and returns element refs
- # Binary: ~300MB Camoufox Firefox fork
- # Dependencies: GTK3, Xvfb, Node.js 18+
- # Config: environment variable CAMOUFOX_EXECUTABLE
- ## Usage Notes
- 1. **Close tabs** after finishing to free browser resources
- 2. **Check snapshots** first to find element refs
- 3. **Search macros** (`@google_search`, etc.) work faster than clicking through home pages
- 4. **Browser auto-restarts** — if you get "Tab no longer exists", create a new one
- 5. **Session isolation** — each tab gets its own browser context, cookies isolated per user
